# Keep the Fly/Docker build context small. The Dockerfile fetches deps, runs
# npm ci, and builds assets inside the image, so none of the build artifacts,
# editor caches, or VCS history below are needed — and this repo is pushed over
# a slow uplink, so a lean context is what lets the remote-builder upload finish.

# VCS + agent/editor state
.git
.gitignore
.claude
.vscode
.vscode-shared

# Elixir/Mix build artifacts (root AND nested per-app, incl. vendored evision)
_build
deps
**/.elixir_ls
**/_build
**/deps

# JS deps (rebuilt by `npm ci` in the image)
**/node_modules

# Crash/dump/temp/coverage/doc artifacts
erl_crash.dump
*.dump
tmp
**/tmp
cover
**/cover
doc
docs
.fly

# Local-only GPU service (Bumblebee/EXLA) — the Dockerfile deletes it anyway.
apps/mehungry_local_ai

# Local env / secrets that must never enter the image.
.env
*.env
